<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Balopwe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Balopwe refers to the sacred quality of kingship in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luba-empire">Luba Empire</a>, believed to be transmitted through the royal bloodline. Those possessing it could claim the right to rule. The concept underpinned Luba royal legitimacy and helped spread Luba-style kingship among neighbouring peoples.</p></div>
